            {
              "id": "DS1705",
              "name": "stale-cross-language-edge",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A declared cross-language edge with a side that at least one analyzer evaluated and every evaluation of that side reports absent, so no analyzer that ran enumerates that side's symbol."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A declared cross-language edge with a side that at least one analyzer evaluated and every evaluation of that side reports absent, so no analyzer that ran enumerates that side's symbol. Emitted by the merge, once per edge, never by an analyzer, so a stale edge is visible rather than silently inert. A dead side paired with an absent side drops its pending finding, and the edge is the reported defect: a misspelled reference must not turn a live pairing into a deletion."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A declared cross-language edge with a side that at least one analyzer evaluated and every evaluation of that side reports absent, so no analyzer that ran enumerates that side's symbol. Emitted by the merge, once per edge, never by an analyzer, so a stale edge is visible rather than silently inert. A dead side paired with an absent side drops its pending finding, and the edge is the reported defect: a misspelled reference must not turn a live pairing into a deletion."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem": {
                  "severity": "error"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS1801",
              "name": "unused-parameter",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A parameter with no reference inside its function body, on a function whose signature is free to change."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A parameter with no reference inside its function body, on a function whose signature is free to change."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A parameter with no reference inside its function body, on a function whose signature is free to change.\n\nThe signature must be free, defined as follows: the function is not a method retained by interface satisfaction, is not a method whose name and signature are those of a method of an exported interface type declared by a package outside the target that the import closure holds, is not used as a value, is not a go:linkname or cgo target, is not a go-fuzz entry point, is not a function the Go test driver runs (a test, benchmark or fuzz test of a test file, or TestMain), and is not a stub whose body is empty or only panics. A function literal or function expression that initializes a variable the program only calls, never passing, storing, returning or assigning it, is called by name and is not used as a value. In Go a function literal that is the callee of the call it is written in, the call of a `go` or a `defer` statement included, is not used as a value, wherever the literal is written. A parameter its body never names is dead whatever the callers, so a published declaration of a library is reported too, with the fixability the vocabulary gives the kind: the signature change is a breaking change. In TypeScript a caller may pass a function used as a value more arguments than it declares parameters, so in such a function whose signature is free but for that use, a parameter its body never reads is reported for deletion when its body reads no parameter after it, and an unread parameter before the last read one is reported for a rename to its name with a leading underscore, which keeps every argument in place and which the compilers' unused-parameter rules read as declared unread, unless its name already starts with one. A parameter of a TypeScript function expression or arrow function that the compiler gives a contextual type, and that carries a type annotation, is not reported for deletion where the inference of the call holding the function may read the annotation, being where the callee is generic and its parameter type at the function's place names a type parameter at the parameter's place, or where the function is written inside an object literal such a call is passed, and it is reported for deletion at `probable` where it carries an annotation no such inference reads, because nothing in the program shows that an outside reader ignores it. Such a parameter is not reported when it is an object binding pattern, because the pattern reads each property it names from the argument and the code that hands the argument may act on that read. No name such a pattern binds is reported either. Any other TypeScript parameter that is a binding pattern is judged by the names it binds: each name the body never reads is reported wherever the pattern stands, because removing it from the pattern moves no argument, except a name beside a rest element of the same object pattern, whose removal changes what that element holds, and the pattern counts as a read parameter when the body reads any name it binds. A rest parameter is judged as the last parameter. A TypeScript `this` parameter declares the type of `this` and receives no argument, so it is never reported. A TypeScript constructor is used as a value where its class is used as a value other than as the callee of a `new` expression or the class an `extends` clause names, and its signature is not free where its class carries a decorator or a parameter of the constructor carries one, because the code that decorator or a container runs may construct the class. A parameter property is read by the write to its member the constructor makes, so it is never reported under this kind, and its member is judged under DS1301. A TypeScript name a parameter binds, whole or through a binding pattern, that starts with an underscore is never reported, because a leading underscore is the spelling unused-parameter rules read as declared unread, and no other name exempts a parameter. A Go parameter named by the blank identifier declares no name a body could read and is never reported."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem": {
                  "severity": "warning"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS1802",
              "name": "unused-receiver",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A named method receiver with no reference inside the method body."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A named method receiver with no reference inside the method body. Go permits a method with no receiver name, so the fix deletes an identifier and changes no signature."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A named method receiver with no reference inside the method body. Go permits a method with no receiver name, so the fix deletes an identifier and changes no signature.\n\nNone beyond the rule. Deleting a receiver name changes no signature, so a method retained by interface satisfaction, a method used as a value and a stub are reported as any other method is."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem": {
                  "severity": "warning"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS1803",
              "name": "unused-result",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A result value that no call site of the function uses, on a function whose signature is free to change."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A result value that no call site of the function uses, on a function whose signature is free to change."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A result value that no call site of the function uses, on a function whose signature is free to change.\n\nThe same free-signature rule as unused-parameter, plus a closed-world condition: every call site of the function must be in the loaded graph, because an unknown caller may consume the result, so the kind reports only for a function whose callers are all visible. A call that is the operand of an await expression written as a statement of its own uses a result whose type has a member named then, a promise or another thenable, because the caller sequences on it, and discards any other result. A call written as a statement of its own, or as the operand of void, discards its result whatever its type."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem": {
                  "severity": "warning"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS1805",
              "name": "unreachable-statement",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A statement that control flow cannot reach, at the precision the language's compiler applies to the same construct."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A statement that control flow cannot reach, at the precision the language's compiler applies to the same construct."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A statement that control flow cannot reach, at the precision the language's compiler applies to the same construct."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
